:: story.aManWasHere
{=
(storylet: when
    $story's lock does not contain "story.aManWasHere"
)

(metadata:
"title", "A Man Was Here"
)


($funcMainContent: [{<!--_mainReading hook-->

($funcReveal: "A man", "man") used to be here.

<!--trigger to ?sometimes-->
(set: _trigger to ($funcChainTrigger: "aManSometimes", 5, "sometimes"))

|man)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "Where is he now?", "where") |where)[Gone, by your doing. You must have succeeded._trigger]]

|man)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "Why was he here?", "why") |why)[He followed, like a moth to a flame. Maybe he wanted to live. Maybe he would have died otherwise - so he believed._trigger]]

|man)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "What was his name?", "name") |name)[You |cannot>[($funcReveal: "cannot", "recall")] recall. |recall)[It does not matter anymore. Names can be shed like skin - painfully._trigger (t8n:"dissolve")+(replace: ?cannot)[do not want to]]]]

|man)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "Who was he?", "who") |who)[A //model//, beautiful once, but he withered, as you currently are. Flesh is sadly prone to decay._trigger]]

|man)[
<br>
($funcReveal: "What was he to you?", "what") |what)[As it appeared to most, he was one half of a whole, and you were the other. An easy mistake to make, more difficult to correct._trigger]]

|sometimes)[
<br>
Sometimes, you can still feel his presence. You can even ($funcReveal: "//smell//", "stink") him.]

|stink)[
<br>
The whole apartment stinks. It is flooded with //his// trash, //his// rot. Anyone can tell that this ($funcReveal: "has been a man's place.", "mainDone")]


}],

[{<!--_mainDone hook-->

($funcOutLink: "Assess the damage.", "Behold...", "story.apartmentStudioDirty", [{
    <!--lock-->
    ($funcLock: (passage:)'s name)
}])


}],

false )